{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <iomanip>\n#include <cctype>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <limits>\n#include <cassert>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\nconst i64 MOD = 1000000007;\n\ntemplate<typename T>\nT gcd(T a, T b) {\n    return b == 0 ? a : gcd(b, a % b);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    std::cin.tie(nullptr);\n    std::cout.tie(nullptr);\n\n#ifndef ONLINE_JUDGE\n    std::freopen(\"input.txt\", \"r\", stdin);\n    std::freopen(\"output.txt\", \"w\", stdout);\n#endif\n\n    int T = 1;\n    while (T--) {\n        double x, y, n;\n        cin >> x >> y >> n;\n\n        double target = x / y;\n        i64 best_num = 0, best_den = 0;\n        double best_error = numeric_limits<double>::max();\n\n        if (y <= n) {\n            best_num = static_cast<i64>(x);\n            best_den = static_cast<i64>(y);\n        } else {\n            for (i64 d = static_cast<i64>(n); d >= 1; --d) {\n                double tmp = d * target;\n                i64 num = static_cast<i64>(round(tmp));\n\n                double frac = static_cast<double>(num) / d;\n                double err = fabs(frac - target);\n\n                if (err < best_error) {\n                    best_error = err;\n                    best_num = num;\n                    best_den = d;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        i64 g = gcd(best_num, best_den);\n        best_num /= g;\n        best_den /= g;\n\n        cout << best_num << \"/\" << best_den << \"\\n\";\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n\n        int T = 1;\n        while (T-- > 0) {\n            String[] line = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n            double x = Double.parseDouble(line[0]);\n            double y = Double.parseDouble(line[1]);\n            double n = Double.parseDouble(line[2]);\n\n            double target = x / y;\n            long best_num = 0;\n            long best_den = 0;\n            double best_error = Double.MAX_VALUE;\n\n            if (y <= n) {\n                best_num = (long) x;\n                best_den = (long) y;\n            } else {\n                for (long d = (long) n; d >= 1; --d) {\n                    double tmp = d * target;\n                    long num = Math.round(tmp);\n\n                    double frac = (double) num / d;\n                    double err = Math.abs(frac - target);\n\n                    if (err < best_error) {\n                        best_error = err;\n                        best_num = num;\n                        best_den = d;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            long g = gcd(best_num, best_den);\n            best_num /= g;\n            